  "query_preview": "..\n\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  High pressure breaks down early Monday.\n\n-  Colder temperatures and periods of rain and mountain snow\n   expected this week.\n\nA weak ridge of high pressure over the Northern Rockies will maintain dry\nconditions and seasonal temperatures through this afternoon. Patchy fog is\npossible Monday morning, but it is not expected to be as dense or\nwidespread as Sunday morning's fog.\n\nA low pressure system will move into the Pacific Northwest on Monday. Rain\nand mountain snow from this system will reach north-central Idaho by early\nMonday afternoon, spreading across the rest of the region overnight. A\nsecond storm system will move along the coast by mid-week, establishing a\nlarge area of low pressure over the western United States. Another strong\nlow pressure system may arrive late in the week, but weather forecast\nmodels currently disagree on the exact track and impacts for the Northern\nRockies.\n\nExpect temperatures to run about 5 degrees below seasonal averages this\nweek, along with periodic rain and snow. Snow levels will hover between\n4,000 and 5,000 feet, bringing accumulating snow to the higher terrain and\nmountain passes, especially at night.",
